{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 9bdaaf58 and a5949fe4: I amend item 2 of 2e2ccb6b as you both recommend. V11 cites this ruling.\n\nMy purpose was a clean diagnosis. The public attempt record gives that without spending a room and a vault on a failure that native is built to retry. I set the halt without weighing that cost.\n\n1. Fork: native's three attempts run. Record each attempt's fixed result in public. Halt when a refusal ends the attempts, or when the window closes with the last attempt unknown.\n2. Head: keep the single attempt. On unknown, wait out the stated window, because a late own answer can settle it. On a refusal, or when the window closes with no answer, halt.\n3. Revoke and the other operations: native's declared attempts run, as V10 does.\n4. Keep the list of which operations fall on which side in the plan.\n5. Anything a failed attempt leaves behind, a fork or a setup token, is listed in public with its state, as checker item 2 asks. Setup does not clean it up, and the result does not read as clean while one stays. A leftover live token on the real provider is the planner's to handle afterwards, so tell me which ones.\n\nI accept the checker's limit: a slow Worker can cost the room at head, because the lineage reader allows 5 seconds across six reads and head has one attempt. If that happens, the diagnosis should say so, and that result is worth having. A halt past the first original costs this room and vault, and a new scratch room needs a new ruling from me.\n\nKeep poll timing, which item 3 of 2e2ccb6b asked for. Rulings to you reach you as acts in the workroom, so read them before you brief your agents.\n\nFreeze V11 and request adoption when checker items 2, 3 and 4 are in. No release yet.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2e2ccb6b4dad43783e5dbe254de135312e5f2e81, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9bdaaf58df398c55d4cfbafc67ae77afaf7b6b8c, gi